{"id":"622160874","kind":"article","title":"「好奇心」具有负面涵义","author":"Susan Edelman","original_authors":["Susan Edelman"],"original_source_urls":["https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Curiosity_has_bad_connotations"],"publisher":"Jarrett Ye","column":"认知基石 & 教育培训","date":"2023-04-19","updated":"2023-04-19","votes":7,"comment_count":0,"minutes":1,"chars":522,"keywords":["好奇心","学习动机","探索式学习","语言框架"],"summary":"文章指出，“好奇心”一词在早期心理学与日常语境中可能带有贪求新奇的负面含义，而科学研究中的用法较中性；作者认为这种语言联想可能使教育者低估探索动机。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/622160874","restoration":null,"toc":[],"html":"<p data-pid=\"CTw8c2ji\">阅读 <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/SuperMemo_Guru\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">SuperMemo Guru</a> 时，你会经常读到关于<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Learn_drive\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">学习内驱力</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>的内容，而很少读到关于好奇心的。 这都是因为<b>好奇心</b>具有的负面内涵。 不了解好奇心及其口头含义，已经导致了如「<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Curiosity_is_not_a_priority\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">好奇心不是教育中的优先事项</a>」这样非常有害的说法！</p><p data-pid=\"-m62bDuw\">Susan Edelman 注意到：</p><blockquote data-pid=\"LkmGQaHx\">在 1950 年之前，人们从社会功能角度看待好奇心，例如：为了新鲜感而急切或贪婪地了解新事物。在早期的心理学文献中，好奇心一词具有负面含义。 科学术语「好奇心」更为中性。</blockquote><hr/><p data-pid=\"gpzQQTbr\">引用的摘录来自以下<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/References\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">参考资料</a>：</p><p data-pid=\"lxcZlLFP\">标题：<b>Curiosity and Exploration</b></p><p data-pid=\"qNh5nZ_C\">作者：Susan Edelman</p><p data-pid=\"rh7rv1hs\">链接：<a class=\"external\" href=\"http://www.csun.edu/~vcpsy00h/students/explore.htm\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">http://www.</span><span class=\"visible\">csun.edu/~vcpsy00h/stud</span><span class=\"invisible\">ents/explore.htm</span><span class=\"ellipsis\"></span></a></p><p data-pid=\"lU0_8UY